From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: fe14 <engine@localhost>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 23:26:29 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 06/21] frontend: Fire Emblem Fates' first run starts with the
 port's picks

The Fates port's owner chose (its docs/DECISIONS.md F-041, engine build
OK 2026-11-19) 60 fps battles, the 3D at 3x with the slider up to 8x, and
the top screen 16:9 together with the extra that draws the 3D for it, as
the defaults of the shipped program. Zakuro keeps its settings in
%APPDATA%\zakuro\settings.toml whatever --data says, and the extras were a
player cheat file copied by hand, so a default needs a change here:

- zakuro-core enhancements.txt lists the port's four extras for
  0004000000179800 rev0 (60 fps battles, 16:9 top screen, faster battles
  150%, 60 fps story scenes, test), the same codes as the port's
  tools/extras/usa_extras.py build writes (our own words, no original
  bytes). They are built-in enhancements: never in the player's cheat
  file, on and off by name in settings.toml, and off puts the bytes back.
  Their credit line names the port, not the GBAtemp thread.
- Settings::load() starts from Settings::first_run() when there is no
  settings file (NotFound only): the defaults, plus for Fates its own
  top shape 16:9 and the enhancements 60 fps battles and 16:9 top screen.
  Resolution stays the default 3 and the slider 1..=8. Faster battles and
  60 fps story scenes stay off. A settings file that is there, even an
  empty or unreadable one, is used as before and never replaced; the
  first run's settings are written when Zakuro first saves (console id).

Tests added (settings, enhancements); not run here, only the port's
standalone program was built (owner's OK covers that build only).
